# 10. Correct Tool Selection

Today's training reinforced using the right tool for the symptom.

| Symptom                       | Tool                   |
| ----------------------------- | ---------------------- |
| Windows performance problem   | Task Manager           |
| Windows service               | `services.msc`         |
| System/application error      | Event Viewer           |
| Hardware/driver               | Device Manager         |
| Startup problem               | `msconfig`             |
| Group Policy issue            | `gpupdate`, `gpresult` |
| Windows network configuration | `ipconfig /all`        |
| DNS issue                     | `nslookup`             |
| Network path                  | `tracert`              |
| Linux processes               | `ps`, `top`, `htop`    |
| Linux RAM                     | `free -h`              |
| Linux disk                    | `df -h`                |
| Linux service                 | `systemctl`            |
| Linux service logs            | `journalctl`           |

### Principle

> The best first troubleshooting tool is the one that provides the most relevant evidence for the reported symptom.

