# 14. Behavioral Interview Practice

## Question

**How do you approach troubleshooting a problem you have not seen before?**

### Professional Answer

> I first gather information and clarify the symptoms. I then identify possible causes and start with the simplest and safest troubleshooting steps. I use available documentation, system tools, and logs to collect evidence rather than making assumptions. Once I identify the likely cause and have authorization to make the change, I apply the appropriate fix and verify the result with the user. I document the work and escalate the issue if it is outside my technical scope or authorization.

